-- title:
--   Valuative criterion over the j-line for the H₁ moduli ring
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring, let $q$ and $\ell$ be primes and $M'$ a nonzero natural number, with $5 \le \ell$ and both $\ell$ and $M'$ invertible in $A$. Assume the three variable-change compatibilities over arbitrary $A$-algebras $T$: `hℓ`, that the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-condition on a quadruple $D=(x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q)$ (namely $(x_P,y_P)$ satisfies the affine equation, $(W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi_\ell)(x_P)=0$, and $(x_Q,y_Q)=(x_P,y_P)$) is preserved by $D \mapsto D.\mathrm{variableChange}\,C$; `hM`, that `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` is preserved by `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k)`; and `hL`, that divisibility of `inLineMulPoly W ℓ n x` by $h$ passes to the transformed polynomial and the transformed abscissa. Assume further a family $\mathcal G$ of relative group laws on the graded projective models of Weierstrass curves with invertible discriminant, chord-and-tangent in the sense of admitting a compatible points evaluation (`IsChordTangent`) and with identity section given in the origin chart by $x/y \mapsto 0$, $z/y \mapsto 0$ (`IsOriginIdentity`); a transport $\mathcal T$ of raw Drinfeld pairs along $A$-algebra maps and variable changes preserving the level-$q$ Drinfeld-basis condition and satisfying `IsSectionTransport`; and the hypotheses `hVC`, `hCO` that variable changes and coefficient maps are implemented by graded ring maps of the projective-model rings with the stated irrelevant-ideal condition. Let $P_0$ be an abstract package representing the moduli datum of `rigidDataH1Pow A ℓ M' q hℓ hM hL 𝒢 𝒯`, whose points over an $A$-algebra $T$ are the classes, modulo Weierstrass variable change, of curves over $T$ with unit discriminant equipped with cyclic kernel generators at the prime powers dividing $M'$, a $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-point, a level-$q$ Drinfeld pair and the `IsGamma1Link` divisibility; thus $P_0$ consists of an $A$-algebra $B_0$ and a universal point through which every point factors by a unique $A$-algebra map. Finally let $K$ be a field that is an $A$-algebra, let $V \subseteq K$ be a valuation subring which is a discrete valuation ring and contains the image of $A$, and let $\varphi : B_0 \to K$ be an $A$-algebra map with $\varphi(j_0) \in V$, where $j_0$ is the $j$-invariant of the universal point. Then $\varphi(b) \in V$ for every $b \in B_0$.
--
--   This is the discrete valuative criterion for the fine moduli ring of the $H_1$-type level structure over the $j$-line: boundedness of the $j$-invariant forces boundedness of all coordinates. It feeds the integrality statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.isIntegral_adjoin_j0_levelModuliPackageAbs_rigidDataH1Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.isIntegral_adjoin_j0_levelModuliPackageAbs_rigidDataH1Pow), which expresses that $B_0$ is integral over the subring generated by $j_0$.
